  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IBRD Hybrid Capital contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UK will make a &#xa3;100m (c.$127m) hybrid capital contribution to the World Bank&#x2019;s IBRD. This will unlock &#xa3;800m in extra lending from the IBRD for Middle Income Countries (MICs). This extra financing will be used for projects that will (1) help MICs achieve the Sustainable Development Goals and reduce poverty and (2) tackle global challenges, such as climate mitigation and pandemic preparedness. Hybrid Capital is a new financing instrument for the World Bank, allowing countries to voluntarily increase their subscribed capital / funding to the IBRD without the need for wider funding round by all countries. It does not carry the same rights / privileges as capital through a routine IBRD capital increase. It is not a &#x2018;core contribution&#x2019; to the World Bank, therefore, though the UK could convert its Hybrid Capital into a core contribution as part of a future IBRD funding round.</narrative>
  </description>
